course: dictionary
lesson: 9231
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives song three meanings: a short piece of music with words that you sing, the act of singing, and the musical sounds a bird makes. The context tells you which meaning the writer means.
explain: «The blackbird sang its song at dawn.» Here song means the musical sounds a bird makes, because the subject is a bird. Always ask: who or what is doing this, and what is it doing? That tells you which meaning fits.
explain: «She burst into song as the bus pulled away.» Burst into song means she suddenly started singing. Song here means the act of singing, not a particular tune.
explain: Some phrases use song in a special way. «He bought the old bike for a song» means very cheaply, and «all that song and dance about nothing» means a big fuss. You cannot work these out from each word alone, so learn the whole phrase.
fact: A song is a short piece of music with words that you sing.
fact: «Song» can also mean the act or art of singing, as in «burst into song».
fact: A bird's song is the musical sounds it makes, and birdsong helps birds attract mates and defend their area.
fact: «For a song» means very cheaply.
fact: «Song and dance» means a big fuss.
exercise: «The blackbird sang its song at dawn.» What does song mean here? | A piece of music with words you could write down | The act of dancing | A type of bird | *The musical sounds a bird makes
exercise: «She burst into song as the bus pulled away.» What does burst into song mean? | She fell asleep on the seat | She began to shout angrily | She began to dance in a circle | *She suddenly started singing
exercise: «He bought the old bike for a song.» What does for a song mean? | *Very cheaply | With a loud noise | Very expensive | Without any music
test: In music lessons, Mia learns a new song with a chorus and a rhyme. Which meaning of song is this? | A kind of dance | The sounds a bird makes | The act of singing | *A short piece of music with words that you sing
test: «The shop made a song and dance about its sale, but nothing really changed.» What does song and dance mean here? | A silly song for children | A happy party with music | *A big fuss | A kind of dancing
exam: Kenji reads «The thrush's song filled the garden.» Which meaning of song fits, and what clue tells him? | *The bird's musical sounds, because a thrush is a bird and it fills the garden | The act of singing, because Kenji is singing | A short piece of music with words, because songs have words | A big fuss, because the garden is busy
